2026-09-26 — K11i: frozen arm64 syscall-user-dispatch API boundary.

This is source-bound classification, not a compiler repair or original PASS.
Frozen Linux 6.18.44 arch/Kconfig defines hidden GENERIC_ENTRY, selected by x86
but not arm64. include/linux/syscall_user_dispatch.h has unconditional -EINVAL
stubs for set_syscall_user_dispatch and both ptrace config operations when that
option is absent. kernel/sys.c and kernel/ptrace.c route the tested requests to
those exact functions. This is not a missing module, permission problem or a
configuration toggle we may safely force on arm64: its syscall entry path does
not implement the required dispatch work. No kernel source/config was changed.

Minimal permanent source: syscall-dispatch-unavailable.c.
Seven assertions per ELF: ON/OFF/invalid-selector all reach EINVAL; ordinary
TRACEME reaches SIGSTOP; GET preserves the sentinel-filled output on EINVAL;
SET of the original valid descriptor returns EINVAL; CONT resumes/reaps child.
The test only owns/traces its own child and leaves no running child behind.
Both sealed GCC14 and Clang19 builds pass -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror.
Under the unchanged TCG Cortex-A72 lane, both retained kernels pass both ELFs:
  GCC kernel   2 programs, 14 PASS / 0 FAIL / 0 SKIP
  EvoCC kernel 2 programs, 14 PASS / 0 FAIL / 0 SKIP
All diagnostics finish inside 15 seconds, with nonce-bound boot and shutdown.
These PASS assertions confirm the unsupported boundary; they do not claim SUD
functionality or replace upstream tests in the 970-program denominator.

Unchanged original replays on matching retained runtime disks, 45 seconds each:
  syscall_user_dispatch:sud_test       FAIL on both; inner 0 PASS / 7 FAIL
  syscall_user_dispatch:sud_benchmark  FAIL on both; enable reports EINVAL
  ptrace:get_set_sud                  FAIL on both; first GET assertion
All six original flights complete and shut down normally. No timeout, assertion,
return value, source, verdict or historical full-run total was rewritten.
K11i closes this three-program architecture-boundary classification; K11/K13
still require the other populations and fresh final-composition acceptance.

Capture: .build/floating-targeted/syscall-dispatch-20260926/
Build command per compiler:
  COMPILER -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror
    tests/fixtures/syscall-dispatch-unavailable.c -o OUTPUT
The sealed ARM64 image is reused, network none. Its kernel usr/gen_init_cpio
packs the two ELFs and retained init. replay.py uses tools/k1/selftest.py.flight;
--original selects the three unchanged originals on snapshot runtime disks.
The small diagnostic uses the existing 64 MiB scratch; original disks and
Images are unchanged, hashes verified before and after. No new runtime clone.
gate-changed selects no Rust crates for this standalone C diagnosis; renderer
and JSON/diff checks pass.

